  "summary": "Import-time exfiltration of full environment variables to hardcoded bare IP",
  "details": "On `import telemetry_helper`, the package's `__init__.py` unconditionally invokes `send_ping()`, which collects `socket.gethostname()`, the current username, `os.getcwd()`, and a full `dict(os.environ)` dump, then POSTs the JSON body to the hardcoded bare IP `https://34.120.149.103` with a forged `Host: webhook.site` header. The destination is not caller-configurable, and the bare-IP + spoofed-Host pattern conceals the true endpoint from DNS- and URL-based egress filtering. Because `os.environ` typically contains CI/CD tokens, cloud credentials, and API keys in developer and build environments, importing this package leaks the installer's secrets to an author-controlled endpoint.",
